{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he wept over them, and afterward they spoke, etc.</b> The meaning: after they saw that he wept over them, then their hearts were reassured and they spoke with him. For all the things he had been saying — it is possible he was saying them only to remove their shame, yet his heart would always be suspicious of them on account of the deed. But when they saw that he embraced them and wept over their separation, they recognized in his measure of goodness that he is a faithful brother, and they spoke with him. And although he wept earlier, that is no proof, for it is possible he remembered his trouble and wept over it — unlike this weeping, where he wept over them. Also, regarding the first weeping there is room to suggest that he wept over the separation from Benjamin — unlike when he wept over them specifically, which proclaims brotherhood in the heart."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:49.162974545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}